- Explicit loop over bandwidths in LGKDE.compute_kde_scores performing the same per-bandwidth Gaussian computation and accumulation, which is also directly vectorizable: [
  /workspace/Learnable Kernel Density Estimation for Graphs [lQxSGO2kBa]/supplementary/LGKDE-SupplementaryMaterial/LGKDE-Codes/model.py:355-361
]
- Explicit loop over bandwidths in DGMMD._mmd_single_embedding_sup to compute exp(-dist/bw) and take maxima; can be vectorized by stacking bandwidths and using broadcasting then a reduction over the bandwidth axis: [
  /workspace/Learnable Kernel Density Estimation for Graphs [lQxSGO2kBa]/supplementary/LGKDE-SupplementaryMaterial/LGKDE-Codes/model.py:240-249
]
- Explicit loop over bandwidths in DGMMD._compute_mmd_sup computing per-bandwidth kernel means, which is amenable to vectorization with broadcasting and reductions: [
  /workspace/Learnable Kernel Density Estimation for Graphs [lQxSGO2kBa]/supplementary/LGKDE-SupplementaryMaterial/LGKDE-Codes/model.py:285-293
]
- Additional explicit nested loops over graph indices to compute pairwise MMD between graphs, indicating further potential for vectorization across graph pairs (though more involved): [
  /workspace/Learnable Kernel Density Estimation for Graphs [lQxSGO2kBa]/supplementary/LGKDE-SupplementaryMaterial/LGKDE-Codes/model.py:135-147, 158-167
]
